      "side": 1,
      "message": "With the mergeable gate removed, an open change with `submittable\u003dtrue` that turns out to have a merge conflict will now show \"Ready to submit\" for the 1-3s while mergeability loads, and then flip to \"Merge Conflict\" (and with the header class fix, the border goes green -\u003e red). That\u0027s a false positive the old gate was implicitly protecting against.\n\nCould we avoid claiming READY_TO_SUBMIT until mergeability is known? Showing ACTIVE in the meantime is fine (optimistic upgrade later is OK, a wrong \"ready\" claim isn\u0027t):\n\n```ts\nif (change.submittable \u0026\u0026 options.mergeable !\u003d\u003d undefined) {\n  states.push(ChangeStates.READY_TO_SUBMIT);\n}\n```\n\nand update the new test case `{mergeable: undefined}` + `submittable \u003d true` to expect `[ChangeStates.ACTIVE]`.",
